The "Digital Capture Volume" is alsa-lib softvol plugin element, and
works globally.  In the case of a digital mic (i.e. usually without a
volume control), sometimes this is the only effective control.

> Strangely, though, the '* Mic' controls in the PLAYBACK section of alsamixer 
> do change the recording properties somewhat (volume being the main factor). 

If you mean about "Mic Boost" or such, then it's a known
(long-standing) bug in ALSA mixer interface.  This appears twice, for
playback and capture, but only the playback one works.


